   To me,  the need/usage of confirmations is an admission that the
   hardware to interface with is limited.  After all,  do you really attack
   someone by moving into them?  Of course not. 

And that's where the interface is wrong.  You shouldn't use the same
keys to fight and to move.  

What you can do:

	Use the control keys to move, if possible.

What could be done in 3.1:

	Create an option, which makes "f <dir>" or maybe
        "<shift><dir>" the only way to fight. If you try to move into
	a monster, nothing should happen, just like when you try to
	move into a wall.


